{% extends 'tabs/base-slide.twig' %}

{% set id = 'ladb_cutlist_slide_mcft_diagram_pack' %}
{% set out = true %}

{#
    THE PAPER PACK — every board's cutting diagram in ONE print job.

    Amit, 2026-09-03: "printing cutting diagrams and labels one by one is
    tedious task." On a study unit that is five sheet-good groups, each needing
    the modal opened, the options confirmed, the pack computed and the sheet
    printed. Five identical answers to reach one job's worth of paper.

    LABELS ARE NOT IN HERE, and that is his constraint rather than an omission:
    "i print labels on pre cut self adhesive 6x12 stickers. part list, cutting
    diagrams on plane paper." Different media cannot share a print job, so the
    labels keep their own action — which already batches every part in one pass.

    The part list is not separate either: each diagram carries its own group's
    part list already, so the pack is the part list, board by board, next to
    the layout it belongs to.
#}

{% block headerInner %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {% include 'tabs/cutlist/_header-extra.twig' %}
{% endblock %}

{% block headerHeadingInner %}
    {{ 'tab.cutlist.cuttingdiagram.title'|i18next }}
    <small>| {{ packs|length }} {% if packs|length == 1 %}board group{% else %}board groups{% endif %}</small>
{% endblock %}

{% block headerToolsInner %}
    <button id="ladb_btn_print" class="btn btn-primary"{% if packs|length == 0 %} disabled{% endif %}><i class="ladb-opencutlist-icon-print"></i> {{ 'default.print'|i18next }}</button>
    &nbsp;
    <button id="ladb_btn_close" class="btn btn-default"><i class="ladb-opencutlist-icon-close"></i> {{ 'default.close'|i18next }}</button>
{% endblock %}

{% block containerInner %}
    {{ parent() }}

    {% if packs|length == 0 %}
        <table class="ladb-page"><tr><td>
            <div class="alert alert-warning">No sheet-good group produced a cutting diagram.</div>
        </td></tr></table>
    {% endif %}

    {% for pack in packs %}
        {#
            One board group per page. `with pack` merges the group's own
            sheets/options/errors over the shared context, so the body renders
            exactly what the single-diagram slide would have rendered for it —
            same file, so the two cannot drift.
        #}
        <div class="ladb-mcft-pack-part"{% if not loop.first %} style="page-break-before: always;"{% endif %}>
            <h3 style="margin:18px 0 6px;">
                {{ pack.group.material_name|escape('html') }}
                <small>/ <strong>{{ pack.group.std_dimension }}</strong></small>
            </h3>
            {% include 'tabs/cutlist/_cuttingdiagram-2d-body.twig' with pack %}
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
